Z||000005||88 Database Nut||12-17-2001||09:54 PM||||Hi Guys, I've been out of town on business and just found this thread.  It's good to hear people talking about Fiero databases, 'cause I sure haven't done that lately!  Too much travel and work lately, but I'm hoping to change that in the future.<P>Anyway, that's a good idea about a database for all years.  Actually, Ray Paulk kind of already does that!  If you goto his TTop registry site, you'll find that he accepts info on any year fiero, not just '88 TTop cars.  He also runs the Indy Fiero Registry, so he's much more on top of the database thing than I am.  Let me take a couple of paragraphs and tell anyone who isn't familiar with the '88 Database Project what it's all about.<P>Basically, I'm trying to document the fates of all 26,402 '88 Fieros built.  It's a crazy thing, but I started it a couple of years ago after wondering what had become of the cars built around the same time as mine.  I also felt that this needed to be done, and maybe I could do something to give back to the Fiero community.  Someday I hope to meet up with the fieros built just before and after mine and take a "family" portrait!  <P>But, back to the project.  It has evolved into a database of info on around 2800 of the 26,402 cars built.  I accept any and all info on '88s, but really need only the following:  the Vin, Exterior and Interior colors (and wheel color for GTs), Tranny option, and status (alive, dead, junkyard, parts car, etc).  This is a car database, not an owners database, and if a owner wishes anonymity I am more than happy to enter the car's info without any owner info.  I like to get as complete a picture of a car as possible (mileage, options, where purchased, date on the ALDL connector, etc), but any info is better than no info.  <BR>It's not that I don't like other years, but I decided to focus on '88s for the following reasons.  One, I have a couple and I wanted to find out more about them and their siblings, and the changes which occured throughout the model year.  It really is true that small changes took place during the production run.  Some early cars have '87 parts on them (trunklids, for example), and the 5 speed tranny underwent a minor change around the midpoint of production.  Two, I decided, rightly or wrongly, that the '88s would be more easily documented, since there should be more of them still around (because they are the newest of the models, and because they are generally considered more collectible (and therefore are more likely to be preserved, as shown by the number of stored and low mileage cars out there)).  I don't know that I really think that ANY year or model Fiero will be a collectible.  I hope they will be, and I know I consider ALL year Fieros to be worthy of documenting.  <P>It's just that, after tromping around junkyards for several years, and seeing 50 to 1 of the '84-'87 year cars to every '88, I formed the opinion that I could NEVER get enough info on the earlier cars to do a database of them justice.  Heck, it's probably too late for many of the '88s already!  But, I felt I had to try, and so I am trying, when able, and hope you understand why I am doing it for the '88s only.  I want this project to be as complete as possible, and I just didn't feel that taking on the whole 370,000 production run would allow me to do that.  I definately am not trying to discourage you, but I have found that 26,402 is a VERY large number when trying to track down info on every one of them, not to mention compiling the info as well.  TWELVE times 26,402 is so big it really is overwhelming. Who needs Carl Sagan's billions and billions, try counting to 26,402 and see what That's like!<P>So, Please let me know if I can help you out, but be careful what you wish for. I have around 6000 84-87 vins I can send your way, and boy-howdy, thasalotta numbers!!!!!<P>Goodnight and Goodluck from a tired '88 Database Nut, I'll catch up with ya and this thread in the morning.  <P>John,  John.Willhoff@LMCO.com||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierokid87||12-18-2001||01:25 AM||||Yes a Data base would be a great Idea.  Ill go collect some vins that I know of (like 10 Fiero between two bone yards.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG">   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid-xmas-sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||8Ball||12-18-2001||07:23 AM||||Hey that is cool. I still think I want to give this database a go. My wife and I are archive nuts, so this should be a great project for the two of us. So everyone please send me you vin's and info for 84-87 Fiero's to cybercoven@chartertn.net. And if you could please title the mail with VIN in it. That way it will go into the right folder. Thanks everyone.<P>E.B.<BR>And Database Guy,<BR>Thanks for all the help and anymore you can offer. Just send me those 6000 vin's if you wish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks again,<BR>Randy||||reg||1
